# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in from the Spotify for Developers dashboard.
#
# The client id is a public value: the authorisation code flow with PKCE proves
# the client with a per-attempt code verifier instead of a secret, so there is
# no secret to keep here. It still lives outside git so a fork points at its own
# Spotify app rather than inheriting this one's user allowlist and rate limit.
VITE_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=

# `1` runs the app on fixtures: no Spotify account, no tokens, no network. The
# session, the Web API and the playback device are all replaced by stand-ins in
# `src/fake/`. `npm run dev:fake` sets this for one run without editing a file.
VITE_FAKE_SPOTIFY=
